//
// A LIVE REFERENCE ACROSS A GROW IS REFUSED (`@FR-B-Ref-Reshape`, `@FR-B-Disturb`): loft will not
// quietly downgrade a `&` to a copy, so where it cannot honour the write it declines the program.
//
// @falsified-at: none — a conformance guard; the refusal held on the tree it landed on.
// CHANNEL: the expected diagnostic.
// ARMED: no instrument.
// WITNESS: the diagnostic names the container and the reference.
// HOLDS: the view spelling in the sibling file compiles on both trees.
// @EXPECT_ERROR: cannot grow `v` while `c` references a place inside it

struct P { n: integer }

fn main() {
  v = [P { n: 1 }, P { n: 2 }];
  c = &v[0];
  v += [P { n: 3 }];
  c.n = 9;
  println("{v[0].n}");
}
